[V3] |H|=6 boundary: does the level-7 sieve fail (residual genuine)?
   |H|=6 sets tested: 1500; level-7 sieve FAILED on 0 (0.0%).
   => |H|=6 is below the sieve threshold: residual = covering sets with <=6 mult of 7.

[Residual] After level-7 sieve, LRC(14) reduces to:
   covering 13-sets with <= 6 multiples of 7  (=> <= 6 multiples of 14).
   This is STRICTLY smaller than THM-571's |M14|<=6 residual:
